1 "Consider the vectors\n\n![](images/9f/9f5f9de266fac1e593ea58a3406ff88ccecb3a64963d55367297404360771d83.png)\n\nIf $x_1 \\mathbf{a}_1 + x_2\\mathbf{a}_2 + x_3\\mathbf{a}_3 = \\mathbf b,$ then what is $x_1+x_2+x_3?$" 13194139534328 17592186045417 false] [17592186119669 1074 "Since $\\mathbf{b}$ is a linear combination of vectors $\\mathbf{a_1}, \\,\\mathbf{a_2}$ and $\\mathbf{a_3}$ with coefficients $x_1,\\, x_2$ and $x_3,$ respectively, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {x}_{1} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n![](images/4d/4d3cb5eb82dd012582c78fc2c1201c62f99779d92974aba2a61f5a6bce8b91b9.png)\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{3}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3 = 2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(2) = 1 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_2 = -1,\n$$\n\nand substituting $x_3=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_1+2(2) = 1 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_1 = -3.\n$$\n\nSo the solution of the system is $x_1=-3, x_2=-1, x_3=2,$ which means\n\n$$\n-3 \\mathbf{a_1}- \\mathbf{a_2} +2 \\mathbf{a_3}= \\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nx_1+x_2+x_3=-3-1+2=-2.\n$$" 13194139534328 17592186045417 false] [17592186119669 1074 "Since $\\mathbf{b}$ is a linear combination of vectors $\\mathbf{a_1}, \\,\\mathbf{a_2}$ and $\\mathbf{a_3}$ with coefficients $x_1,\\, x_2$ and $x_3,$ respectively, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {x}_{1} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n![](images/9b/9bf913744317fab321cf9f2e01da732853a52a4fd7948c65da596ae4706f6dce.svg)\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{3}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3 = 2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(2) = 1 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_2 = -1,\n$$\n\nand substituting $x_3=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_1+2(2) = 1 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_1 = -3.\n$$\n\nSo the solution of the system is $x_1=-3, x_2=-1, x_3=2,$ which means\n\n$$\n-3 \\mathbf{a_1}- \\mathbf{a_2} +2 \\mathbf{a_3}= \\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nx_1+x_2+x_3=-3-1+2=-2.\n$$" 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186119805 1038 #edb/ref 17592186419107 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186120045 1050 960.0 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186120293 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186120293 1071 "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186120293 1071 "Consider the vectors\n\n$a_{1} = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}, a_{2} = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}, b = \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nIf $x_{1}a_{1} + x_{2}a_{2} = b$, then what is $x_{1} + x_{2}$?" 13194139534328 17592186045417 false] [17592186120293 1074 "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1} \\\\ -{x}_{1} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ {x}_{2}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation we get ${x}_{2}=2$, which we substitute into the second equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} & =3 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+2 & =3 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=-1$ and ${x}_{2}=2$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & =5 \\\\ -(-1)+2(2) & =5 \\\\ 5 & =5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=-1$ and ${x}_{2}=2,$ which means\n\n$$\n-{a}_{1}+2{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-1+2=1.\n$$" 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186121034 1064 "Consider a vector $\\mathbf{u}$ which is given in terms of the vectors $\\mathbf{v_1}$ and $\\mathbf{v_2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}3}{\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v_1}}+({\\color{red}-2}){\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v_2}} = \\mathbf{u}\n$$\n\nHere, we say that $\\mathbf{u}$ is a **linear combination** of the vectors ${\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v_1}}$ and ${\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v_2}}$ with coefficients ${\\color{red}3}$ and ${\\color{red}-2}$ respectively. \n\nIn general, a linear combination of $n$ vectors $\\mathbf{v_1},\\mathbf{v_2},\\dots,\\mathbf{v_n}$ is the *weighted sum*\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}x_1}\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_1}+{\\color{red}x_2}\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_2}+\\cdots + {\\color{red}x_n}\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_n} = \\mathbf{u},\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\color{red}x_1},{\\color{red}x_2},\\dots,{\\color{red}x_n}\\in\\mathbb{R}.$ We say that $\\mathbf{u}$ is a linear combination of the vectors $\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_1},\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_2},\\dots,\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_n}$ with coefficients (or *weights*) ${\\color{red}x_1},{\\color{red}x_2},\\dots,{\\color{red}x_n},$ respectively.\n\nFor instance, \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the linear combination of vectors $\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_1},\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_2},\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_3}$ with coefficients ${\\color{red}2}, {\\color{red}0}, {\\color{red}\\dfrac{1}{2}},$ respectively." 13194139534328 17592186045417 false] [17592186121034 1064 "Consider a vector $\\mathbf{u}$ which is given in terms of the vectors $\\mathbf{v_1}$ and $\\mathbf{v_2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}3}{\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v_1}}+({\\color{red}-2}){\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v_2}} = \\mathbf{u}\n$$\n\nHere, we say that $\\mathbf{u}$ is a **linear combination** of the vectors ${\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v_1}}$ and ${\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v_2}}$ with coefficients ${\\color{red}3}$ and ${\\color{red}-2}$ respectively. \n\nIn general, a linear combination of $n$ vectors $\\mathbf{v_1},\\mathbf{v_2},\\dots,\\mathbf{v_n}$ is the *weighted sum*\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}x_1}\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_1}+{\\color{red}x_2}\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_2}+\\cdots + {\\color{red}x_n}\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_n} = \\mathbf{u},\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\color{red}x_1},{\\color{red}x_2},\\dots,{\\color{red}x_n}\\in\\mathbb{R}.$ We say that $\\mathbf{u}$ is a linear combination of the vectors $\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_1},\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_2},\\dots,\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_n}$ with coefficients (or *weights*) ${\\color{red}x_1},{\\color{red}x_2},\\dots,{\\color{red}x_n},$ respectively.\n\nFor instance, \n![](images/ff/ff71636b9b5a34fec4de37b5e924c1c6bc3765c1ee823b325f5b0e01c0dc472a.svg)\nis the linear combination of vectors $\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_1},\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_2},\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v_3}$ with coefficients ${\\color{red}2}, {\\color{red}0}, {\\color{red}\\dfrac{1}{2}},$ respectively." 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419101 1080 "No solution" 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419101 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419101 1083 #uuid "1715fd90-ec78-5246-a305-0bc79c6d6201" 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419102 1080 "-6" 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419102 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419102 1083 #uuid "6737f66e-5883-51c4-b5ee-f853d82f7a52" 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419103 1080 "3" 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419103 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419103 1083 #uuid "9beb45ed-f52f-5f55-aced-c84e6915532b" 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419104 1080 "6" 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419104 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419104 1083 #uuid "b56988f7-12ae-5627-bee9-3cfcc596e9cb" 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419105 1080 "\\frac{10}{3}" 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419105 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419105 1083 #uuid "ceaa277a-f8cc-5c5e-8f5b-4a33f950d108" 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419106 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419101 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419106 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419102 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419106 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419103 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419106 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419104 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419106 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419105 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419106 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419106 1077 "selection" 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419106 1078 #edb/ref 17592186419101 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419106 1079 #uuid "d86debef-7386-5ca7-a1b7-df6c6f4c242e" 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419107 1068 #edb/ref 17592186419106 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419107 1069 "q-73923" 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419107 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419107 1071 "Find $m$, if $5{a}_{1}+m{a}_{2}=0$ and \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419107 1072 #uuid "80bf8c74-6292-5b04-9a45-fc39723fd232" 13194139534328 17592186045417 true] [17592186419107 1074 "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $m$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{a}_{1}+m{a}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 5[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+m[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ m[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-5[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ m[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-30 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the first components, we get \n\n$$\n-5m=-30\\,⟹\\,m=6.\n$$\n\nBut then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-30 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]\\ne [\\begin{aligned}-30 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there is no $m$ such that $5{a}_{1}+m{a}_{2}=0.$" 13194139534328 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-1715fd90-ec78-5246-a305-0bc79c6d6201" 17592186419101 "answer-6737f66e-5883-51c4-b5ee-f853d82f7a52" 17592186419102 "answer-9beb45ed-f52f-5f55-aced-c84e6915532b" 1759218